8. Glossary
Term	Definition
Dynamic Array	An array that automatically resizes. Python lists are dynamic arrays.
Stack	Memory region for local variables and function call frames. Stores references (pointers).
Heap	Memory region for dynamically allocated objects. Python list data lives here.
Volatile Memory	RAM — data is lost when the process ends.
Serialization	Converting in-memory objects to a storable format (e.g., JSON) for persistence.
IPO Model	Input-Process-Output — the fundamental architecture of every program.
enumerate()	Python built-in that returns (index, value) pairs. Implements Iterator Protocol.
Amortized O(1)	Occasional expensive operations (resizes) averaged out — most appends are O(1).
Primary Key	Unique identifier for a database row. Represented by dict['id'] in this project.
Sharding	Breaking one large dataset (list) into smaller sub-lists across multiple servers.

